0016 — named font faces: a class literal picks a face with `font-[name]`,
and the build bakes that face's slots from files it was told about.

Upstream bakes every slot from one regular/bold pair (plus the mono face);
a composition that sets a display face, a body face and a CJK face has to
be three compositions. This keeps the default pair as it is and adds faces
beside it. Declaration-layer only: the core indexes slots and never knew
which file a slot came from, so nothing under engine/ changes except one
constant.

What the patch adds, by file:

- `framework/compiler/tailwind.ts`: the `font-[name]` token (name matches
  /^[a-z][a-z0-9-]*$/, exported as FONT_FACE_NAME). A face's (px, weight)
  pairs are always dynamic slots, keyed with the face, so the pinned table
  and every existing slot number are untouched; a face takes precedence
  over `font-mono`. `fontSlotInfo`/`fontSlotPlan` carry `face`, and the
  `FONT_SLOTS` mirror names it — only on face slots, so a build with no
  face writes the mirror it always wrote.
- `framework/compiler/bake-font.ts`: `BakeOptions.faces` (name -> files);
  a face slot bakes from its face, and a slot naming an undeclared face is
  refused with the declared names, rather than baked from the default pair.
- `tools/build.ts`: `--font-face-regular=<name>=<path>` and
  `--font-face-bold=<name>=<path>`; a face declared with one weight is a
  build error.
- `contracts/spec/spec.ts`, `engine/core/src/spec.rs` (regenerated):
  MAX_FONT_SLOTS 64 -> 128, so several faces fit. A slot index still fits
  the u8 in the atlas header and GLYPH_RUN; each unused slot is one
  `Option<Atlas>`.
- `tests/tailwind.test.ts`, `tests/font-bake.test.ts`: slot allocation per
  face, precedence over mono, the name rule, a face baked from its own file
  and the refusal of an undeclared one.

`git apply` skips everything above the first `diff --git`.

